From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:40:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: ~190 CSS properties on style objects, currentStyle
 getters, document colors, queryCommand* (3012)

IHTMLStyle, IHTMLStyle2..6 and IHTMLCSSStyleDeclaration/2 had 487 accessors that
returned E_NOTIMPL, so script such as style.borderRadius = "5px" or
style.listStyleType failed. Every BSTR and VARIANT property of them now has a
style table entry (name, dispids, IE10 compat flag) and goes through the
Gecko style declaration like the properties that already worked
(listStyleType, borderRadius, boxShadow, textOverflow, captionSide, emptyCells,
the -ms-animation family, and so on). length and the numeric properties stay as
they were.

IHTMLCurrentStyle getters for the same properties return the computed value.

IHTMLDocument2 fgColor, linkColor, vlinkColor and alinkColor map to the body's
text, link, vLink and aLink (with the IE defaults when unset).
queryCommandSupported, Enabled, State and Indeterm answer from the command
tables, which now also know the names Bold, Italic, Underline, Justify*,
SelectAll, Delete, ForeColor and InsertHorizontalRule for execCommand.

Tests added to style.c and dom.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS

